# Normalize line endings on commit.
#
# `* text=auto` alone normalizes the index but still checks out CRLF on Windows.
# That is not cosmetic here: a CRLF shebang in docker-entrypoint.sh makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the container
# exits with a misleading "no such file or directory". `eol=lf` pins the working
# tree too, so a Windows checkout cannot reintroduce it.
#
# This file does not exist upstream — it is excluded from the publish manifest as
# dev-side tooling — so it has to live here on its own. Without it, a Windows
# clone of the upstream repo checks out CRLF and the first commit here would bake
# a broken entrypoint into history.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh       text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.opml     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
